      "message": "Bah, looking again at the spec, this still probably isn\u0027t quite right. For example, if the guest issues an `FFA_VERSION` call, I don\u0027t think the spec defines an `FFA_ERROR` return code and so this will lead to confusion.\n\nSo perhaps this should actually be rolled up in the `SMCCC_RET_NOT_SUPPORTED` case above? That means we\u0027ll behave the same way as `!VM_FFA_SUPPORTED(vcpu)` in the case that the host hasn\u0027t negotiated the version. WDYT?",
