      "writtenOn": "2025-11-06T09:06:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think the spec actually _requires_ the guest to issue an `FFA_VERSION` call. For example, maybe it has the version hardcoded or it receives it via firmware (e.g. devicetree). In any case, we should return a spec-compliant error code in this case and so I think the easiest thing is to return `SMCCC_RET_NOT_SUPPORTED` by extending the check above to:\n\n```\nif (!is_ffa_call(func_id) || !VM_FFA_SUPPORTED(vcpu) || !smp_load_acquire(\u0026has_version_negotiated)) {\n\tsmccc_set_retval(vcpu, SMCCC_RET_NOT_SUPPORTED, 0, 0, 0);\n\treturn true;\n}\n```",
      "parentUuid": "cc0507c7_ba9feef4",
